213		// ServeMux treats any empty path segment (the doubled slash in
214		// /v1/documents//..., /v1/devices//sessions or
215		// /v1/sessions//documents/...) as an unclean path and answers with a 307
216		// HTML redirect (a 404 in a real client). The API contract is a 400 JSON
217		// error for an empty identifier, so intercept those paths before the mux
218		// sees them. A trailing slash empties the final id of the device/session
219		// routes and is rejected there for the same reason; the document routes
220		// keep their pre-existing ServeMux behavior.
221		return emptyIDGuard(mux)
222	}
