Wait — do I even need lastValue dedupe? Pending swept at registration are all sent. Later, each wake → drain outbox; entries appended since last drain are new commits; each commit appends exactly one entry per state-changing commit. Committed states could repeat in value? A state-changing commit always changes the merged value, but two successive commits could... counter: 5 → 8 → 8? No: to commit a change, value must strictly increase for the device; sum strictly increases. So counter values strictly increase across state-changing commits. GSet: union strictly grows. So successive committed states are always distinct. But non-successive? Counter sum always grows; gset union always grows — merged states form a strictly increasing sequence, never repeat. So no dedupe needed at all! Every outbox entry is a distinct new state. 

